{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01T6zsnYb37oHcWWi938CXZz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014AxjzBVP7PDSngREJ6DJLH","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1252,"cache_read_input_tokens":121817,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1252},"output_tokens":40,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4cb46183-2e7c-4dbc-b888-4ae03f7bba08","uuid":"e89a8732-cdef-4759-ae63-3a4d14e45f0c","request_id":"req_011Cb7Rx1zd8rRQ48SMfsrev"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014AxjzBVP7PDSngREJ6DJLH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Baseline Workflow Benchmarks\n2\t\n3\tThis directory stores the Phase 0 baseline required by `## Phase 0: Fork Foundation` in [docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md:566). The purpose is to measure the current Lattice workflow hot paths before the fork-build phases change identity resolution, event capture, retrieval, or metrics behavior.\n4\t\n5\tThe benchmark suite is implemented in [daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/baseline_workflows.rs](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/baseline_workflows.rs:1). It uses a deterministic temp-workspace fixture, runs the current workflow logic with `cargo bench`, and rewrites `baseline_metrics.json` on every successful run.\n6\t\n7\t## Re-run\n8\t\n9\tRun the two required validation commands from the repo root:\n10\t\n11\t```bash\n12\tcd daemon && cargo build --release --benches\n13\tcd daemon && cargo bench --bench baseline_workflows -- --warm-up-time 1 --measurement-time 3\n14\t```\n15\t\n16\tThe second command regenerates [baseline_metrics.json](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json:1).\n17\t\n18\t## Metrics File\n19\t\n20\t`baseline_metrics.json` is the machine-readable snapshot consumed by later regression work. Each object includes:\n21\t\n22\t- `name`: workflow benchmark name\n23\t- `p50_us`, `p95_us`, `p99_us`: latency percentiles in microseconds\n24\t- `bytes_returned`: serialized response size for the benchmarked workflow\n25\t- `candidate_count`: top-level result count captured with the payload size\n26\t- `commit_sha`: git commit recorded when the snapshot was captured\n27\t- `recorded_at`: unix timestamp captured at bench time\n28\t\n29\tThe baseline is intentionally compact. It is the reference point for the later success claims in `## Measurable Success Criteria` from [docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md:875), especially the discovery-call and irrelevant-read reductions.\n30\t\n31\t## Budget Interpretation\n32\t\n33\tPhase 1 and Phase 2 define hot-path budgets that later work must validate as deltas against this baseline:\n34\t\n35\t- Identity resolution must add no more than 2 ms P99 to hot-path tool calls.\n36\t- Event write must add no more than 5 ms P99 to hot-path tool calls such as `prepare_change` and `get_context_capsule`.\n37\t\n38\tThose targets come from the Phase 1 and Phase 2 definition-of-done text in [docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md:609). This Phase 0 suite measures pre-Phase-1 behavior only. Later tasks should compare their new numbers against this file rather than replacing the meaning of the baseline.\n39\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4cb46183-2e7c-4dbc-b888-4ae03f7bba08","uuid":"9171d305-8b79-46ad-a01d-98dcbc6117cb","timestamp":"2026-05-17T03:28:23.595Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/README.md","content":"# Baseline Workflow Benchmarks\n\nThis directory stores the Phase 0 baseline required by `## Phase 0: Fork Foundation` in [docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md:566). The purpose is to measure the current Lattice workflow hot paths before the fork-build phases change identity resolution, event capture, retrieval, or metrics behavior.\n\nThe benchmark suite is implemented in [daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/baseline_workflows.rs](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/baseline_workflows.rs:1). It uses a deterministic temp-workspace fixture, runs the current workflow logic with `cargo bench`, and rewrites `baseline_metrics.json` on every successful run.\n\n## Re-run\n\nRun the two required validation commands from the repo root:\n\n```bash\ncd daemon && cargo build --release --benches\ncd daemon && cargo bench --bench baseline_workflows -- --warm-up-time 1 --measurement-time 3\n```\n\nThe second command regenerates [baseline_metrics.json](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json:1).\n\n## Metrics File\n\n`baseline_metrics.json` is the machine-readable snapshot consumed by later regression work. Each object includes:\n\n- `name`: workflow benchmark name\n- `p50_us`, `p95_us`, `p99_us`: latency percentiles in microseconds\n- `bytes_returned`: serialized response size for the benchmarked workflow\n- `candidate_count`: top-level result count captured with the payload size\n- `commit_sha`: git commit recorded when the snapshot was captured\n- `recorded_at`: unix timestamp captured at bench time\n\nThe baseline is intentionally compact. It is the reference point for the later success claims in `## Measurable Success Criteria` from [docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md:875), especially the discovery-call and irrelevant-read reductions.\n\n## Budget Interpretation\n\nPhase 1 and Phase 2 define hot-path budgets that later work must validate as deltas against this baseline:\n\n- Identity resolution must add no more than 2 ms P99 to hot-path tool calls.\n- Event write must add no more than 5 ms P99 to hot-path tool calls such as `prepare_change` and `get_context_capsule`.\n\nThose targets come from the Phase 1 and Phase 2 definition-of-done text in [docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md:609). This Phase 0 suite measures pre-Phase-1 behavior only. Later tasks should compare their new numbers against this file rather than replacing the meaning of the baseline.\n","numLines":39,"startLine":1,"totalLines":39}}}
