{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R9kEZoY8uqG9vWJtcbLP4H","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# T01 — Phase 0 — Fork-or-extend decision doc with evidence\n2\t\n3\t**Phase:** 0\n4\t**Type:** foundation\n5\t**Model class:** advanced\n6\t**Depends on:** none\n7\t**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 0: Fork Foundation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-0-fork-foundation)\n8\t**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n9\t\n10\t## Goal\n11\t\n12\tThis task produces the binding fork-or-extend decision that every subsequent task in this build assumes. The spec gates Phase 0 on a \"fork only if necessary\" rule with four named gate conditions; this document evaluates each gate condition against current Lattice code evidence, names a branch or repo, and records the decision. The decision must precede any structural change because `depends_on` chains assume the layout, crate boundaries, and migration policy that this document selects. Without an explicit, evidence-backed decision, later phases would be free to silently diverge.\n13\t\n14\t## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n15\t\n16\t> \"Phase 0 ends with an explicit fork/extend decision before any structural code changes begin. Fork if any of the following are true: the memory graph schema changes require breaking the existing `memories` table in a way that cannot be migrated without a full rebuild; the identity model requires changing the primary key or graph edge representation in a way that invalidates existing indexed data; the event log requires a new storage file or WAL mode incompatible with the current daemon's SQLite usage; two or more of the above apply and sharing a codebase would require sustained compatibility shims across all phases.\"\n17\t\n18\t> \"If none of those conditions hold, extend in place on a long-lived branch and skip the repo split. Document the decision and the evidence for it before Phase 1 begins.\"\n19\t\n20\t## Inputs\n21\t\n22\t- Dependency outputs: none (this is the first task).\n23\t- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n24\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` (current memory schema and storage)\n25\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/graph/` (current identity and edge representation)\n26\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` (current SQLite usage and WAL mode)\n27\t  - `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-structured-memory.md`\n28\t  - `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md`\n29\t  - `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-storage-and-search-backends.md`\n30\t  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/context.md` §4 \"Fork-or-extend decision\"\n31\t- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (no broken windows, single source of truth); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/AGENTS.md` (backward compatibility discipline).\n32\t\n33\t## Steps\n34\t\n35\t1. Read `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md` §Phase 0 in full to internalize the gate conditions verbatim.\n36\t2. Inspect `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/storage.rs` and `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/schema.rs` (or equivalent) and enumerate every column on the `memories` table; record which Phase 3 fields are additive vs. breaking.\n37\t3. Inspect graph primary keys and edge representation in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/graph/`; determine whether the Phase 1 identity model invalidates existing indexes.\n38\t4. Inspect current SQLite connection setup in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` and confirm WAL/journal mode; determine whether a new `events.db` file can coexist without WAL incompatibility.\n39\t5. Evaluate each of the four gate conditions against the evidence and record a `met`/`unmet` verdict per condition with file/line citations.\n40\t6. State the decision (`extend on long-lived branch` or `fork to new repo`) and name the branch or repo (e.g. `feat/cognitive-workspace`)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4cb46183-2e7c-4dbc-b888-4ae03f7bba08","uuid":"385e563b-3f84-4f39-9f11-97973c0effc5","timestamp":"2026-05-17T03:33:09.455Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T01.md","content":"# T01 — Phase 0 — Fork-or-extend decision doc with evidence\n\n**Phase:** 0\n**Type:** foundation\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** none\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 0: Fork Foundation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-0-fork-foundation)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task produces the binding fork-or-extend decision that every subsequent task in this build assumes. The spec gates Phase 0 on a \"fork only if necessary\" rule with four named gate conditions; this document evaluates each gate condition against current Lattice code evidence, names a branch or repo, and records the decision. The decision must precede any structural change because `depends_on` chains assume the layout, crate boundaries, and migration policy that this document selects. Without an explicit, evidence-backed decision, later phases would be free to silently diverge.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 0 ends with an explicit fork/extend decision before any structural code changes begin. Fork if any of the following are true: the memory graph schema changes require breaking the existing `memories` table in a way that cannot be migrated without a full rebuild; the identity model requires changing the primary key or graph edge representation in a way that invalidates existing indexed data; the event log requires a new storage file or WAL mode incompatible with the current daemon's SQLite usage; two or more of the above apply and sharing a codebase would require sustained compatibility shims across all phases.\"\n\n> \"If none of those conditions hold, extend in place on a long-lived branch and skip the repo split. Document the decision and the evidence for it before Phase 1 begins.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: none (this is the first task).\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` (current memory schema and storage)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/graph/` (current identity and edge representation)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` (current SQLite usage and WAL mode)\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-structured-memory.md`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-storage-and-search-backends.md`\n  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/context.md` §4 \"Fork-or-extend decision\"\n- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (no broken windows, single source of truth); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/AGENTS.md` (backward compatibility discipline).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md` §Phase 0 in full to internalize the gate conditions verbatim.\n2. Inspect `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/storage.rs` and `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/schema.rs` (or equivalent) and enumerate every column on the `memories` table; record which Phase 3 fields are additive vs. breaking.\n3. Inspect graph primary keys and edge representation in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/graph/`; determine whether the Phase 1 identity model invalidates existing indexes.\n4. Inspect current SQLite connection setup in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` and confirm WAL/journal mode; determine whether a new `events.db` file can coexist without WAL incompatibility.\n5. Evaluate each of the four gate conditions against the evidence and record a `met`/`unmet` verdict per condition with file/line citations.\n6. State the decision (`extend on long-lived branch` or `fork to new repo`) and name the branch or repo (e.g. `feat/cognitive-workspace`).","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":74}}}
